{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Affordable short read sequencing\"\n",
        "author: \"jk\"\n",
        "description: \"In praise of Illumina's NovaSeq\"\n",
        "date: \"2024-11-17\"\n",
        "format: \n",
        "  html: default\n",
        "toc: true\n",
        "categories: [other]\n",
        "jupyter: \n",
        "  kernelspec:\n",
        "    name: \"conda-env-scvi-tools-py\"\n",
        "    language: \"python\"\n",
        "    display_name: \"scvi-tools\"\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "If there is one thing that has gotten **cheaper** in this economy, it would be short read next generation sequencing. During my grad research, I did a few bulk RNA-seq and ChIP-seq experiments and I remember holding my breath before seeing each quote in the mid four figures. Those numbers included library prep kit cost, too, so they ran a bit higher. Notwithstanding, Illumina's NovaSeq has made this type of sequencing much more affordable[^1]. See the plot below comparing cost (in CAD) per million reads between various machines and flow cells. \n"
      ],
      "id": "ab5c3710"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "  \"Machine\": [\"NextSeq500\", \"NextSeq1000\", \"NextSeq2000\", \"NextSeq2000\",\n",
        "  \"NovaSeqX\", \"NovaSeqX\", \"NovaSeqX\"],\n",
        "  \"$/1M\": [9.01, 2.88, 2.35, 2.15, 2.17, 1.90, 1.51],\n",
        "  \"Machine-Flow\": [\"Next-High\",\"Next-P2\",\"Next-P3\", \"Next-P4\", \"Nova-10B\",\n",
        "  \"Nova-25B\", \"Nova-10B\"]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "sns.barplot(\n",
        "    data=df,\n",
        "    x='Machine-Flow',\n",
        "    y='$/1M',\n",
        "    hue='Machine'\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Mean Proportion\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Proportion of Cell Types by Condition\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "ec476a64",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "[^1]: Assuming you already bought one for [$1.2M](https://genohub.com/ngs-sequencer/3/illumina-novaseq-x-plus/), or have access to it through a local genomics core. The latter being the more likely scenario.  \n",
        "\n",
        "::: center\n",
        "\\\\ (•◡•) /\n",
        ":::"
      ],
      "id": "bdfdd2b5"
    }
  ],
